<item name='HelpECategories'><text>2. Database Custodian Guide</text></item>
<item name='HelpESubCat'><text>Customizing the Application</text></item>
<item name='HelpFCategories'><text>2. Guide de gardien de base de données</text></item>
<item name='HelpFSubCat'><text>Customizing the Application</text></item>
<item name='HelpDocNumber'><number>7</number></item>
<item name='HelpSubCatNumber'><number>2</number></item>
<item name='HelpEHelpText'><richtext>
<pardef id='1' leftmargin='0.8125in' rightmargin='60%'/>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>There are TWO DISTINCT STEPS to adding a new employee:</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	1. Adding him/her to the Access Group</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	2. Adding him to the Project List.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font size='14pt' style='bold underline' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20' color='blue'/>1. Adding an employee to the Access Group</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Access groups are used to provide limited access to different sets of users.  There are four different access levels:</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<pardef id='2' leftmargin='1.5000in' rightmargin='60%' list='bullet'/>
<par def='2'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Read only access: no edit capability.  They do not have access to the Admin area.  These people are READERS.</run></par>
<pardef id='3' leftmargin='2.4500in' rightmargin='60%' firstlineleftmargin='1.5000in'
 list='bullet'/>
<par def='3'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Placing orders: read, write and limited edit (this is most of the staff).  They cannot edit an order after the order number has been assigned by the Admin person.  They do not have access to the Admin area.  These people are EDITORS.</run></par>
<pardef id='4' leftmargin='2.9000in' rightmargin='60%' firstlineleftmargin='1.5000in'
 list='bullet'/>
<par def='4'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Principal Investigators: same rights as those placing orders but they have read access to the Admin area.  These people are INVESTIGATORS.</run></par>
<par def='2'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Database Managers: full read/write/delete access to all areas of the database.  These people are ADMIN.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>The Access Groups are managed by entering the Admin area and then clicking on Access Groups from the navigator.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<pardef id='5' leftmargin='1.5000in' rightmargin='60%'/>
